    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When Asciidoctor converts a document, it delegates to the converter to convert each node (block or inline element) in the document as it visits each node in document order (though it’s the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "#content"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " method on a block that continues the traversal of its child nodes). Asciidoctor then combines the result of all those calls to produce the output document."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To convert a node, Asciidoctor calls the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "convert"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " method on the converter and passes in the node. In some cases, it also passes in an extra transform value (e.g., "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "embedded"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ") to differentiate between different uses cases for a node of the same context. When Asciidoctor is using a converter that extends "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Asciidoctor::Converter::Base"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", the converter will delegate the call to a method whose name starts with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "convert_"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and is followed by the context of the node (e.g., "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "convert_paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ")."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The following table lists the contexts for all the built-in nodes that Asciidoctor converts, along when the name of the method the base converter will look for. Extensions can introduce additional contexts."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
